# Environment configuration.
#
# `SITE_ORIGIN` is the site's canonical origin. It is read by astro.config.mjs at
# build time through src/lib/site-origin.mjs, which also derives `indexable`, and
# it therefore drives the canonical URL, og:url, og:image, the JSON-LD @id graph,
# the sitemap and the `Sitemap:` line in robots.txt at once. It is NOT a PUBLIC_
# variable: it is a build input, not browser configuration.
#
# Leave it unset for a local or preview build — the build then uses the host it
# is served from (VERCEL_URL) or localhost, and is marked noindex with a visible
# non-production notice. A production build must set it to a domain the
# organisation owns; `linkbot.org` is refused, because the organisation does not
# control it. See docs/preview/README.md and docs/preview/domain-migration.md.
#
# SITE_ORIGIN=https://<owned-domain>

# Jobsite supply configuration.
#
# PUBLIC_ variables are inlined into the client bundle by Astro. Never put a
# secret, token or private key in one: a token for the supply call must be
# brokered server-side (see docs/jobsite/supply-integration-handoff.md).

# Canonical Universal Supply API origin. When set, /jobs serves live supply
# through HttpSearchAdapter instead of the labelled fixture set.
# Leave unset to stay in the fixture-backed preview.
# PUBLIC_SUPPLY_API_ORIGIN=
